 \section{Introduction and relevant prior work}
 Adaptive management couples action with learning rather than treating monitoring as an afterthought. Richer published models jointly consider management, surveillance, robustness, and dynamic state change. This note deliberately does less: it makes one payoff identity explicit so a restoration plan cannot hide the cost of committing before learning. The contribution claimed here is only transparent bookkeeping.
